<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened Runtime exceptions for a Developer ID build.

    Electron's renderer is V8, which writes and then executes machine code —
    the first two keys allow that. The third lets the process load libraries
    signed by a different team, which Electron's own frameworks need under
    Developer ID. Without these the app launches to a blank window or not at
    all, and the notary service does not tell you why.

    Microphone: the app records for voice input (see NSMicrophoneUsageDescription).
    Without this entitlement the hardened runtime denies the device silently.

    Nothing here loosens the file system: Labee is not sandboxed, and the
    Developer ID path does not require it — which is the point. The product
    runs a CLI against the person's own files.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
